WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.062 --> 00:00:14.944
Ivy was sitting with Ezra and Glen at morning assembly.

2
00:00:14.964 --> 00:00:17.267
"Listen up!"

3
00:00:17.707 --> 00:00:18.428
Private said.

4
00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:20.950
"Sports Day is next week.

5
00:00:22.011 --> 00:00:27.276
There will be relay races, swimming competitions, and a basketball free throw.

6
00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:31.690
We'll also have a canoe race and a home run derby."

7
00:00:34.232 --> 00:00:34.953
Ivy groaned.

8
00:00:36.273 --> 00:00:39.756
"Why aren't there any drawing competitions?"

9
00:00:41.057 --> 00:00:43.338
Private asked Mango to announce the prize.

10
00:00:44.259 --> 00:00:45.079
Mango grinned.

11
00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:48.301
"All the winners get Frosty Freeze ice cream!"

12
00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.523
The campers cheered.

13
00:00:52.384 --> 00:00:55.846
Ezra, Glen, and the others did the crazy Camp Evergreen dance.

14
00:00:56.987 --> 00:00:58.028
Ivy rolled her eyes.

15
00:00:59.232 --> 00:01:05.975
"This prison camp is so bad, the inmates get excited over ice cream," she thought.

16
00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:09.636
Private pointed to the sign-up sheets on the bulletin board.

17
00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:12.218
Everyone rushed to get in line.

18
00:01:13.258 --> 00:01:15.039
Ivy and the boys stood near the back.

19
00:01:15.059 --> 00:01:18.900
"I don't mind relay races," Ezra said.

20
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.221
"I'm actually a fast runner.

21
00:01:22.222 --> 00:01:25.183
I just imagine bullies chasing me for my lunch money."

22
00:01:26.644 --> 00:01:27.404
Glen grinned.

23
00:01:28.528 --> 00:01:31.049
"Last year I came in fifth place in swimming."

24
00:01:31.069 --> 00:01:35.010
"Fifth?" Ivy stared at him.

25
00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.211
"That's not great."

26
00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:42.092
"My swimsuit was too big," Glen said.

27
00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:45.533
"So, I had to hold it up while I swam.

28
00:01:45.553 --> 00:01:48.114
It fits perfectly this year.

29
00:01:48.754 --> 00:01:50.014
I'm bound to do better!"

30
00:01:53.675 --> 00:01:56.356
Ezra frowned when they finally reached the sign-up sheets.

31
00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.841
"What are we going to do?

32
00:02:00.081 --> 00:02:02.382
Almost every event is full."

33
00:02:02.402 --> 00:02:07.764
"There are three openings for the canoe race," Ezra said.

34
00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:09.365
Glen shrugged.

35
00:02:10.445 --> 00:02:11.606
"It's not my favorite.

36
00:02:12.486 --> 00:02:13.827
But we can do it together."

37
00:02:13.847 --> 00:02:16.468
"Fine," Ivy snapped.

38
00:02:16.488 --> 00:02:19.429
"But there's only one race I want to win."

39
00:02:19.449 --> 00:02:22.010
"Huh?" Glen said.

40
00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:25.611
"The race to get out of here on the last day of camp!"

41
00:02:26.132 --> 00:02:26.632
Ivy said.

42
00:02:27.616 --> 00:02:29.838
Glen wrote their names down for the Yellow team.

43
00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:33.600
"We'll need to practice," he said.

44
00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.442
"We'll be racing against the Red and Blue teams."

45
00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:40.305
As they walked to the lake, Ivy complained again.

46
00:02:40.325 --> 00:02:44.008
"Why are sports such a big deal at camp?

47
00:02:45.169 --> 00:02:49.092
I'm drawing a graphic novel, Zombie Attack at Camp Nevergreen.

48
00:02:49.992 --> 00:02:51.934
I can draw zombies faster than anyone.

49
00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.976
But nobody cares about that skill."

50
00:02:56.444 --> 00:02:58.625
"I don't like sports either," Ezra said.

51
00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:02.766
"But a trip to Frosty Freeze ice cream shop is a big deal."

52
00:03:02.786 --> 00:03:05.406
"Yeah," Glen said.

53
00:03:05.426 --> 00:03:08.187
"They're famous for the Colossal Cone.

54
00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.968
It has four scoops of ice cream!"

55
00:03:10.988 --> 00:03:13.949
"And six toppings," Ezra said.

56
00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:16.569
"Wait!" Ivy halted.

57
00:03:16.589 --> 00:03:21.311
"Are you saying the winners get to leave camp for ice cream?"

58
00:03:22.211 --> 00:03:22.811
She grinned.

59
00:03:22.831 --> 00:03:25.892
"Now that's what I call a prize!"

60
00:03:27.772 --> 00:03:31.233
At the lake Larry sat in a lifeguard chair watching the swimmers.

61
00:03:32.453 --> 00:03:34.134
Other campers paddled in canoes.

62
00:03:35.394 --> 00:03:37.635
Ivy, Glen, and Ezra approached Penelope.

63
00:03:38.855 --> 00:03:40.515
She was supervising the canoers.

64
00:03:40.535 --> 00:03:45.797
"We need to practice for the canoe race on Sports Day," Glen said.

65
00:03:45.817 --> 00:03:48.618
"Great! How much canoeing have you done?"

66
00:03:48.898 --> 00:03:49.738
Penelope asked.

67
00:03:49.758 --> 00:03:52.799
"I did some last year," Glen said.

68
00:03:53.919 --> 00:03:54.559
Ezra nodded.

69
00:03:54.579 --> 00:03:55.779
"Me too."

70
00:03:55.799 --> 00:04:00.377
"Well, I've never been in a canoe," Ivy said.

71
00:04:00.397 --> 00:04:03.537
"Time to get started," Penelope said.

72
00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.939
The kids gathered paddles and life vests from a shed.

73
00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:13.100
"You'll do a dunk test first," Penelope said.

74
00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:16.161
"Go out on the lake and turn your canoe over.

75
00:04:17.241 --> 00:04:19.502
Then climb back in and paddle back to shore."

76
00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:24.763
An empty canoe was tied to the dock.

77
00:04:25.703 --> 00:04:27.924
The kids got in and started paddling.

78
00:04:32.052 --> 00:04:33.133
Ivy was confused.

79
00:04:33.733 --> 00:04:36.434
"Why are we falling out of the canoe on purpose?"

80
00:04:37.494 --> 00:04:40.035
"It's a safety exercise," Glen said.

81
00:04:40.055 --> 00:04:43.817
"Everyone needs to know how to get back in the boat if it capsizes."

82
00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:45.358
Ivy groaned.

83
00:04:45.378 --> 00:04:48.819
"I'm ready to get out right now!"
